From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: convert long TU delays in 64 bits

ieee80211_tu_to_usec() takes and returns an unsigned long, which wraps
on a 32-bit system above 4194303 TU. The delay of an AP removal is the
Beacon interval times the AP Removal Timer minus 1, and both are 16-bit
fields, so a valid element can exceed that. The work then runs early and
removes the link while the AP still serves it. The CSA timeout of a
station has the same overflow with a Channel Switch Count of up to 255.

Convert both delays to ktime in 64 bits.

Fixes: 8eb8dd2ffbbb ("wifi: mac80211: Support link removal using Reconfiguration ML element")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
@@ -2543,6 +2543,13 @@ static inline int __ieee80211_resume(str
 
 /* utility functions/constants */
 extern const void *const mac80211_wiphy_privid; /* for wiphy privid */
+
+/* ieee80211_tu_to_usec() wraps above 4194303 TU on 32-bit */
+static inline ktime_t ieee80211_tu_to_ktime(u64 tu)
+{
+	return us_to_ktime(tu * 1024);
+}
+
 const char *ieee80211_conn_mode_str(enum ieee80211_conn_mode mode);
 enum ieee80211_conn_bw_limit
 ieee80211_min_bw_limit_from_chandef(struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef);
--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -3513,7 +3513,7 @@ ieee80211_sta_process_chanswitch(struct
 	/* we may have to handle timeout for deactivated link in software */
 	now = ktime_get_boottime();
 	csa_time_tu = (max_t(int, csa_ie.count, 1) - 1) * link->conf->beacon_int;
-	link->u.mgd.csa.time = now + us_to_ktime(ieee80211_tu_to_usec(csa_time_tu));
+	link->u.mgd.csa.time = now + ieee80211_tu_to_ktime(csa_time_tu);
 
 	if (ieee80211_vif_link_active(&sdata->vif, link->link_id) &&
 	    local->ops->channel_switch) {
@@ -7834,7 +7834,7 @@ static void ieee80211_ml_reconfiguration
 	sdata->u.mgd.removed_links |= removed_links;
 	wiphy_hrtimer_work_queue(sdata->local->hw.wiphy,
 				 &sdata->u.mgd.ml_reconf_work,
-				 us_to_ktime(ieee80211_tu_to_usec(delay)));
+				 ieee80211_tu_to_ktime(delay));
 }
 
 static int ieee80211_ttlm_set_links(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
